        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That\n- People: French Montana, Machine Gun Kelly, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Roles: American rappers, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Colson Baker was born on April 22, 1990, and he is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio who is better known as MGK or Machine Gun Kelly.\n- Excuse My French is the debut studio album by American rapper French Montana.\n- Excuse My French features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg, among others.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from French Montana's debut studio album Excuse My French in 2013.\n- Pop That features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.",
